course: dictionary
lesson: 5409
title: Labelled: what the word tells you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Labelled comes from the word label, a small sticker or piece of paper that tells you what something is. Read the context: «Chemicals should always stay in their own labelled bottles.» Bottles with a label on them are labelled, so labelled means with a label on it.
explain: The same word can describe a drawing. A «labelled diagram» has the names of its parts written on it, with lines pointing to them. The words around labelled tell you what is being described, and that helps you work out the meaning.
explain: Labelled can also mean described with a name, often unfairly. If someone is «labelled as lazy» after working hard all week, the context tells you the name is not fair. Use the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Labelled is the past form of the verb label: label, labels, labelled, labelling.
fact: «Labelled» can mean with a label on it, as in «labelled bottles».
fact: A «labelled diagram» has the names of its parts written on it, with lines pointing to them.
fact: Graphs need «labelled axes» so you know what each line measures.
fact: Food is labelled with its ingredients, which matters for people with allergies.
exercise: «Chemicals should always stay in their own labelled bottles.» What does labelled mean here? | *With a label on it | Painted bright blue | Hidden under the sink | Empty and cracked
exercise: A drawing of a plant has lines pointing to its roots and leaves, with their names written beside them. What is this drawing called? | *A labelled diagram | A warning sign | A blank sketch | A photo of a garden
exercise: «They were labelled as lazy, though they had worked hard all week.» What does labelled as mean here? | Tested in a laboratory | Sent to bed early | Put in a box with a bow | *Given a name that was unfair
test: «When three boxes are labelled Apples, Oranges and Mixed, every label is wrong.» What does labelled mean in this sentence? | Painted red | Shaken up and mixed | Filled with mixed nuts | *With a label on it that names what is inside
test: Which of these is a labelled diagram? | A blank page for notes | A plain drawing of a dog with no words | *A drawing of a skeleton with each bone named and a line pointing to it | A photo of a bicycle
exam: Why are cleaning products kept in «their own labelled bottles»? | To make them easier to lose | *So each product is clear, safe to use and not mixed up | To look neat on a shelf | To keep them warm
